# SQL & sqlc Conventions

## sqlc Workflow

1. Write SQL in `sql/queries/*.sql` with sqlc annotations
2. Run `make sqlc` to generate Go code in `go/internal/database/`
3. Generated code uses `pgx/v5` — never edit generated files

## Query Annotations

```sql
-- name: GetEntityDescendants :many
SELECT id FROM entity_tree;

-- name: CreateUser :one
INSERT INTO toro_core.users (...) VALUES (...) RETURNING id;

-- name: UpdateUserEmail :exec
UPDATE toro_core.users SET email = $1 WHERE id = $2;
```

Return types: `:one`, `:many`, `:exec`, `:execrows`, `:execresult`

## Schema Conventions

- All domain tables live in `toro_core` schema, ERP mirrors in `shadow_erp`
- Use `UUID` primary keys (generated by default)
- Timestamps: `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()`, `updated_at` via trigger
- Soft deletes where appropriate: `deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ`

## Multi-Tenant Filtering

Always filter by `authorized_entity_ids` for tenant-scoped queries:

```sql
WHERE entity_id = ANY(@authorized_entity_ids::uuid[])
```

For hierarchical access, use the recursive CTE pattern in `GetEntityDescendants`.

## Migrations

- Goose format in `sql/schema/` — sequential numbered files
- Always include both up and down migrations
- Test migrations against a fresh database before committing

## Naming

- Tables: `snake_case`, plural (`toro_core.users`, `shadow_erp.qbo_accounts`)
- Columns: `snake_case` (`entity_id`, `created_at`)
- Query names: `PascalCase` verbs (`CreateUser`, `GetEntityDescendants`, `ListAccountsByRealm`)
